 34CL    32S(3HE,P)                    1977BI04                  ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  {+32}S+1p+1n|){+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+32}S ground state.                 
 34CL c  1977Bi04,1976Bi14: an 18-MeV {+3}He beam was provided from the         
 34CL2c  University of Pennsylvania tandem accelerator. The target was gaseous  
 34CL3c  H{-2}S. Protons were detected on nuclear emulsions in a multi-angle    
 34CL4c  broad range magnetic spectrograph with an energy resolution of 22-25   
 34CL5c  keV. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and    
 34CL6c  spectroscopic factors from DWUCK-DWBA analysis.                        
 34CL c  1976De24: a 24.5-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the Princeton       
 34CL2c  azimuthally varying field cyclotron. The target was CdS with natural   
 34CL3c  {+32}S. Reaction products were detected using a freon-cooled |DE-E Si  
 34CL4c  detector telescope with FWHM=40 keV. Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced    
 34CL5c  levels, L-transfers, J, and |p from DWUCK-DWBA analysis. Also measured 
 34CL6c  {+32}S(|a,d){+34}Cl.                                                   
 34CL c  1972Na23: a 24-MeV {+3}He beam was produced from the MP tandem         
 34CL2c  accelerator of the Max Planck Institut fur Kernphysik in Heidelberg.   
 34CL3c  Targets were PbS on carbon backings. The reaction proons were          
 34CL4c  momentum-analyzed by a multigap magnetic spectrograph and detected     
 34CL5c  using 50-|mm Ilford L4 nuclear emulsions with a resolution of 40 keV.  
 34CL6c  Measured |s(E{-p},|q). Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and         
 34CL7c  spectroscopic factors from zero-range DWUCK-DWBA analysis.             
 34CL c  Others: 1991Ru05 measured cross sections of {+32}S({+3}He,p){+34m}Cl at
 34CL2c  E=4.0-12.0 MeV. 2017Ay03 measured {+32}S({+3}He,p){+34}Cl as a         
 34CL3c  byproduct of {+24}Mg({+3}He,p){26}Al.                                  
